<title>USA: Santa Isabel says holder gets offer.</title>
<headline>Santa Isabel says holder gets offer.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Santa Isabel Sa said Wednesday its controlling shareholder, Eduardo Elberg, received an offer from an independent investor to buy 36.96 percent of the supermarket chain.</p>
<p>The offer would lead to the transfer of control of the Chilean company.</p>
<p>According to Chilean law, the intention to obtain control by an investor must be announced at least five business days before the parties sign the agreement, making a formal announcement expected on May 22, the company said.</p>
